\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Gate v3 (pre-registered) and v4 (post-hoc, frozen, run once) across datasets. KITTI: $t_\mathrm  {rel}$ (\%); EuRoC and TUM-VI: ATE (m). Hand-designed: best pipeline in which we fixed by hand which components are measured and which are learned. Rows marked with a dagger ($\dagger $): released weights of models we did not train, trained with drive 08, so with-08 numbers against OXTS; v3 and v4 were run once, frozen, and v4 was designed without these models. VS-VIO: learned visual policy / full vision. EuRoC, two sequences: five models. TUM-VI: three training seeds (123, 42, 7).}}{9}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:gate}{{4}{9}{Gate v3 (pre-registered) and v4 (post-hoc, frozen, run once) across datasets. KITTI: $t_\mathrm {rel}$ (\%); EuRoC and TUM-VI: ATE (m). Hand-designed: best pipeline in which we fixed by hand which components are measured and which are learned. Rows marked with a dagger ($\dagger $): released weights of models we did not train, trained with drive 08, so with-08 numbers against OXTS; v3 and v4 were run once, frozen, and v4 was designed without these models. VS-VIO: learned visual policy / full vision. EuRoC, two sequences: five models. TUM-VI: three training seeds (123, 42, 7)}{table.4}{}}
